        "original_id": "95a48110-e4d1-51df-b590-6054c0e2b609",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Alberto de Agostini National Park, Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego, South America, Strait of Magellan, Tierra del Fuego, Chile\n- Natural Features: Marinelli Glacier, Marinelli Creek\n- Concepts: tidewater glacier, island, watercourse, headwaters, glacial melt\n\nFacts:\n- Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego was formerly called Isla de Xativa and is also known as Tierra del Fuego, which literally means \"Land of the Fire.\"\n- Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego is an island near the southern tip of South America and is separated from the mainland by the Strait of Magellan.\n- Marinelli Glacier is a tidewater glacier located in Alberto de Agostini National Park on Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego.\n- Marinelli Creek is a watercourse in Tierra del Fuego, Chile, whose headwaters come from the melting of Marinelli Glacier.",
